  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OXFAM: Climate Justice Latin America</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">OXFAM: Klimatr&#xe4;ttvisa Latinamerika</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Bidraget kommer att st&#xf6;dja Oxfams regionala plattform i Latinamerika att utveckla ett program med titeln Klimatr&#xe4;ttvisa f&#xf6;r mer r&#xe4;ttvisa och inkluderande samh&#xe4;llen i Latinamerika, inom ramen f&#xf6;r en tre&#xe5;rig period (oktober 2023 till december 2026). Projektets huvudm&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att bidra till st&#xf6;rre klimatr&#xe4;ttvisa f&#xf6;r befolkningar och samh&#xe4;llen som drabbas h&#xe5;rdast av klimatf&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringarna i Latinamerika och V&#xe4;stindien, baserat p&#xe5; en r&#xe4;ttvis f&#xf6;rdelning av ansvar och deras aktiva deltagande i beslutsfattande utrymmen f&#xf6;r att fr&#xe4;mja finansiering av f&#xf6;rluster och skador och en r&#xe4;ttvis &#xf6;verg&#xe5;ng till h&#xe5;llbara ekonomier och samh&#xe4;llen.
I detta avseende &#xe4;r det &#xf6;vergripande f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntade resultatet av programmet att kvinnor och ungdomar fr&#xe5;n ursprungsbefolkningar och afro&#xe4;ttlingar och lokala samh&#xe4;llen kommer att vara b&#xe4;ttre rustade f&#xf6;r att f&#xf6;rsvara och ut&#xf6;va sina r&#xe4;ttigheter, h&#xf6;ja sina r&#xf6;ster, skydda sina samh&#xe4;llen och b&#xe4;ttre hantera konsekvenserna av klimatf&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringar som de upplever p&#xe5; en daglig basis. Samtidigt kommer Oxfam, tillsammans med lokala och regionala partner, att f&#xf6;rs&#xf6;ka f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra m&#xf6;jligheterna f&#xf6;r kvinnor och ungdomar att f&#xf6;rsvara sina territoriella r&#xe4;ttigheter och st&#xe4;rka sina f&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjningsm&#xf6;jligheter.
D&#xe4;rf&#xf6;r &#xe4;r de specifika m&#xe5;len f&#xf6;r programmet f&#xf6;ljande:
1. Att garantera samh&#xe4;llets deltagande i m&#xe4;tning, tillg&#xe5;ng till och f&#xf6;rvaltning av finansieringsmedel f&#xf6;r f&#xf6;rluster och skador som fr&#xe4;mjar en minskning av k&#xf6;ns-, etniska och generationsm&#xe4;ssiga klyftor.
2. Fr&#xe4;mja institutionella f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringar och nationell offentlig politik f&#xf6;r ratificering och genomf&#xf6;rande av Escaz&#xfa;-avtalet i Latinamerika, med effektiva k&#xf6;ns- och interkulturella tillv&#xe4;gag&#xe5;ngss&#xe4;tt som st&#xe4;rker kvinnors och ursprungsbefolkningars roll i milj&#xf6;beslutsfattandet.
F&#xf6;r att uppn&#xe5; dessa m&#xe5;l kommer Oxfam att arbeta mot f&#xf6;ljande resultat:
Resultat 1. Villkoren f&#xf6;r debatten om klimatr&#xe4;ttvisa, oj&#xe4;mlikheter och r&#xe4;ttigheter informeras av erfarenheter och krav fr&#xe5;n befolkningar och samh&#xe4;llen i Latinamerika, i samband med nationella, regionala och globala klimatf&#xf6;rhandlingsprocesser, inklusive om f&#xf6;rlust och skada och Escazu-avtalet.
Resultat 2. Ungdomar, f&#xf6;respr&#xe5;kare - fr&#xe4;mst urfolk, b&#xf6;nder och afro-descendenter - och andra ber&#xf6;rda grupper &#xe4;r b&#xe4;ttre rustade att f&#xf6;rsvara och ut&#xf6;va sina r&#xe4;ttigheter, skydda sina samh&#xe4;llen och p&#xe5;verka klimatf&#xf6;rhandlingar och politik, inklusive om f&#xf6;rlust och skada och ratificering och genomf&#xf6;rande av Escaz&#xfa;-avtalet.
Resultat 3. Beslutsfattare p&#xe5;verkas att anta och genomf&#xf6;ra &#xe5;taganden f&#xf6;r att s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla samh&#xe4;llets deltagande i m&#xe4;tning, tillg&#xe5;ng till och hantering av finansiering av f&#xf6;rluster och skador och att fr&#xe4;mja ratificering och genomf&#xf6;rande av Escaz&#xfa;-avtalet.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contribution will support Oxfam Regional platform in Latin America to develop a Program entitled Climate justice for more equitable and inclusive societies in Latin America, within the framework of a three-year period activity (October 2023 to December 2026). The project&#x2019;s main objective is to contribute to greater climate justice for populations and communities that suffer the greatest impacts of climate change in Latin America and the Caribbean, based on a fair distribution of responsibilities and their active participation in decision-making spaces to promote loss and damage financing and a just transition towards sustainable economies and societies.
In this sense, the overreaching expected outcome of the program is that women and youth from indigenous and Afro-descendant peoples and local communities will be better equipped to defend and exercise their rights, raise their voices, protect their communities and better manage the consequences of climate change that they experience on a daily basis. At the same time, together with local and regional partners, Oxfam will seek to improve opportunities for women and youth to defend their territorial rights and strengthen their livelihoods.
Therefore, the specific objectives of the program are:
1. To guarantee community participation for the measurement, access and management of financing funds in Loss and Damage that favors the reduction of gender, ethnic and generational gaps.
2. Promote institutional changes and national public policies for the ratification and implementation of the Escaz&#xfa; Agreement in Latin America, with effective gender and intercultural approaches that enhance the role of women and Indigenous Peoples in environmental decision-making.
To achieve these objectives, Oxfam will work towards the following outcomes:
Outcome 1. The terms of the debate on climate justice, inequalities and rights are informed by the experience and demands of populations and communities in Latin America, in the context of national, regional and global climate negotiation processes, including on Loss and Damage and the Escazu Agreement.
Outcome 2. Youth, advocates - primarily indigenous, peasant and afro-descendant - and other affected groups are better equipped to defend and exercise their rights, protect their communities and influence climate negotiations and policies, including on Loss and Damage and the ratification and implementation of the Escaz&#xfa; Accord.
Outcome 3. Decision makers are influenced to adopt and implement commitments to ensure community participation in the measurement, access and management of Loss and Damage funding and to promote the ratification and implementation of the Escaz&#xfa; Accord.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the proposed contribution is to contribute to greater climate justice for populations and communities affected by the impacts of climate change in Latin America and the Caribbean, based on a fair distribution of responsibilities and their active participation in decision-making spaces to promote financing in Loss and damage and a just transition towards sustainable economies and societies.

The work will be carried out at the regional level, with regional partners who have a presence in practically all Latin American countries. Closely linked to regional initiatives, the intervention will have territorial components in the Dry Corridor ecosystem that crosses Guatemala, El Salvador and Honduras, and in the Amazon region of Bolivia, Peru, Colombia and Brazil. The project will also have a global reach, with advocacy actions in Sweden, Denmark, and the EU.

The proposal has the following specific objectives:

1. Guarantee community participation for the measurement, access and management of Loss and Damage financing funds that favors the reduction of gender, ethnic, racial, and generational gaps.

2. Promote institutional changes and national public policies for the ratification and implementation of the Escaz&#xfa; Agreement in Latin America and other protection mechanisms, with effective gender and intercultural approaches that enhance the role of women and Indigenous Peoples in environmental decision-making.</narrative>
  </description>
